  "body": "**Scoped negative result with an algebraic attaining control; no new \u03ba.**\n\nThis resolves one bounded part of PR1337's window-donor handoff. On the pinned PR1297 base word, deleting pivot 440's three early B reads cannot be repaired by at most three restored donor windows, even with arbitrary rational or complex coefficients. Each window spans at most four consecutive source reads inside a no-write segment; helper readers are included. Four explicit windows restore the scalar map on all 704 arbitrary input columns. Their eight added ADD macros are an algebraic control; no physical frame, paid-moment or supplier improvement is claimed.\n\nThe package enumerates 2,758 windows (one zero), 1,611 projective directions and all relevant spans. The separate forward-pulse/integer-rank checker covers 5,177,758 cases. Exact proof, receipts, sources, failure controls, costs, scope and open questions are in `research/complex-p440-window-shocks/`.\n\nReproduce with Python 3.12 and no dependencies:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/complex-p440-window-shocks\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/complex-p440-window-shocks outcome=negative-result`.\n\nValidation passed: registered Python 3.12.13 replay; separate Python 3.14.6 isolated, optimized, read-only relocation; seven semantic/package test groups; Ruff; selected-record integrity. Full cold replay, physical admission, full repository tests, hosted CI and Lean are unrun.\n\nResearch base: `bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f`. Submission refresh: `410026dc5513b87db92ae98571d1d5984c69a983`; selected record and replay hook are unchanged. Sources: PR1337 `abd7384d9a5e35048723512ae70d970909ffd522`, PR1297 `4abf710a7f0d2a46f522f3f13c15769d003f9495`. Only this new package is added.\n\nSeed 34, complex-supplier track. The refreshed overlap scan covered all 791 open PRs and 148 discussions, with no warning; the closest result remains PR1337's narrower two-shock census. Claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1314#discussioncomment-18912079\n\nHanson Sun (@bbMisk), with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Credit Marius-Paul Dumitrean / PR1337, Rohan Arun / PR1297, Jeremy Kothe / PR1274 and the retained lineage. Apache-2.0; predecessor notices retained. No independent human review is claimed.\n",
